Replication package of the doctoral thesis "Reliability of Machine Learning Outputs in Finance"
(Luca Palmacci, Sapienza University of Rome), Chapters 3 to 6.
Copyright 2026 Luca Palmacci

The code is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE). The model of the members' probabilities
implemented in confidex/ is joint work with Stefano Galiani, Davide Petturiti and Barbara Vantaggi:
S. Galiani, D. Petturiti, B. Vantaggi, L. Palmacci (2026), "Bayesian Per-Sample Confidence Estimation
via Decoupled Ensemble Modeling", IPMU 2026.

The systematic review of Chapter 5 (chapter5_systematic_review/) is the work of the author alone. Its
screening records, coding sheet and extraction notes may be reused for research purposes with citation of
the thesis.

Chapter 6 (chapter6_validation_protocol/) includes software developed by Songyan Hou and co-authors
(Time-Causal VAE, https://github.com/justinhou95/TimeCausalVAE), commit
a43effe0125d7c778d0560e4704754991d8e271b, licensed under the Apache License 2.0; the files are in
chapter6_validation_protocol/third_party/tcvae/ and are unmodified (see chapter6_validation_protocol/NOTICE).
Reference: B. Acciaio, S. Eckstein, S. Hou (2026), "Time-Causal VAE: Robust Financial Time Series Generator",
SIAM Journal on Financial Mathematics 17(1), 245-279. The Quant GAN (Wiese et al., 2020) is an independent
implementation of the published paper. The market data of Chapter 6 (Ken French Data Library) are not
redistributed: chapter6_validation_protocol/scripts/get_french.py downloads them.

Third-party data, redistributed unchanged except where stated in chapter4_fraud_experiments/data/README.md:

- chapter4_fraud_experiments/data/ulb_creditcard.csv.gz: "Credit Card Fraud Detection", Machine
  Learning Group of the Universite Libre de Bruxelles and Worldline (Kaggle mlg-ulb/creditcardfraud).
  Made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0,
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/; any rights in individual contents of the database are
  licensed under the Database Contents License (DbCL) 1.0, https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1-0/.
  Reference: A. Dal Pozzolo, O. Caelen, R. A. Johnson, G. Bontempi (2015), "Calibrating probability with
  undersampling for unbalanced classification", IEEE Symposium Series on Computational Intelligence.

- chapter4_fraud_experiments/data/fraud_oracle.csv: "Vehicle Insurance Claim Fraud Detection" (Kaggle
  shivamb/vehicle-claim-fraud-detection), CC0 1.0 as declared by the uploader; line endings converted
  from CRLF to LF. Reference: C. Phua, D. Alahakoon, V. Lee (2004), "Minority report in fraud detection:
  classification of skewed data", ACM SIGKDD Explorations Newsletter 6(1), 50-59.

- chapter4_fraud_experiments/results/tabpfn/: scores returned by the TabPFN service of Prior Labs
  (model TabPFN v3, client tabpfn-client 0.6.1), obtained in October 2026. References: N. Hollmann et al.
  (2025), "Accurate predictions on small data with a tabular foundation model", Nature 637, 319-326;
  L. Grinsztajn et al. (2026), "TabPFN-3: Technical Report", arXiv:2605.13986.

- chapter5_systematic_review/2_screening/: bibliographic metadata (authors, titles, years, sources, DOIs
  and links) of the records retrieved from Scopus, SSRN and arXiv on 10 November 2025, limited to what is
  needed to document the selection. No abstracts, full texts or complete database exports are included.
